    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T15:25:49Z",
    "body": "Diagnostic only, not a proposed fix: [known-failing branch](https://github.com/seelesturm/Camcraft/tree/diagnostic/47-air-prefix) at [8a55c5280d5eb2d2848f272b84ca488a5f995cc4](https://github.com/seelesturm/Camcraft/commit/8a55c5280d5eb2d2848f272b84ca488a5f995cc4), based on `1a882e5fcb648d46bd668d3d5166b2c051eb3301`. Only test modules/registration changed; production selection and safety laws are untouched.\r\n\r\nReproduce from that commit:\r\n```sh\r\ncargo test --locked -p camcraft-motion --lib recovery_ -- --nocapture --test-threads=1\r\n```\r\nObserved: exit 101, **2 controls passed, 1 construction failed, 153 filtered**. The witness generates/replays the real channel entry/opening (1,446 moves; actual/planner stock agree). Its stock-conditioned descending leg passes the rim/stock checks (0 degrees against the unchanged 15.016-degree bite). However, the Hermite floor connector properly crosses two actually emitted opening feeds before reaching the next front. The first crossing is suffix leg 0 against opening piece 1274, near `(11.5002125, 5.3825449)`.\r\n\r\nThe suffix was not walked; subsequent channel advances, band corners/closure, the original full fixtures, budgets and 3-D activation remain unproved. Auxiliary conservative-clearance unknowns are **not** proof of physical collision. This falsifies this finite construction, not every possible noncircular construction.\r\n\r\n**Maintainer decision requested:** under the unchanged landing/engagement/non-crossing laws, what construction or entry/opening ordering should connect an independently stock-cleared landing to the next cutting front without crossing the opening's floor feeds? Alternatively, please clarify the intended existing floor/posted-crossing criterion for this specific witness. I am leaving the production refusal/fallback in place pending that direction; no safety waiver or finished-fix claim.",
