    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T07:32:10Z",
    "body": "Recommended option for the maintainer (one answer closes this question):\n- Recommended: Keep the named refusal and the Offset-ring fallback as the law, and close #47 as `wontfix`; the trochoids share only `ring_entry` of #3743. Cost: effort:low, less than 1 worker-session (no code). Risk: thin channels keep the Offset rings, with a visible note, and #5 and #6 lose the in-planner trochoid.\n- Other: Arcs whose ends sweep the wall strip clean, with a start ramp along the circle extension of each arc. Cost: effort:max, about 2-3 worker-sessions, with no proof yet that it crosses no floor feed.\n- Other: Non-circular loops whose start lies behind the previous envelope. Cost: effort:max, 3 or more worker-sessions; the first finite construction (2026-11-09) crossed two opening feeds.\nAnswer \"recommended\" or name another option.\n",
